---
import Section from '../ui/Section.astro';
import Cluster from '../layout/Cluster.astro';

const layers = [
  {
    name: 'your site',
    sub: '/site.pack',
    size: 'yours',
    sizeLabel: 'size',
    text: 'Packed at build time into one memory-mapped file. Every asset is pre-compressed with Brotli, zstd and gzip, and its ETag is computed in advance. No compression happens at request time.',
  },
  {
    name: 'liamd',
    sub: 'the server',
    size: '5 MB',
    sizeLabel: 'budget',
    hot: true,
    text: 'Thread-per-core on io_uring, with no locks shared between cores. HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2 and HTTP/3. rustls for the handshake, kernel TLS for the bytes. Static files, reverse proxy, and WebAssembly handlers.',
  },
  {
    name: 'liam-init',
    sub: 'PID 1',
    size: '300 KB',
    sizeLabel: 'budget',
    text: 'Mounts, sysctls and entropy. It owns the listening sockets and restarts liamd in under a millisecond if it exits. It can also supervise one app process of your own.',
  },
  {
    name: 'kernel',
    sub: 'Linux LTS',
    size: '9 MB',
    sizeLabel: 'budget',
    text: 'No loadable modules. Drivers for virtio, NVMe, AWS ENA, Google gVNIC and common server NICs only. io_uring, kTLS and BPF built in. Tracks upstream stable releases.',
  },
  {
    name: 'hardware',
    sub: 'or hypervisor',
    base: true,
    text: 'x86_64 and aarch64. Firecracker, Cloud Hypervisor, QEMU, AWS, GCP, Hetzner, or a server in a rack.',
  },
];

const removed = ['shell', 'package manager', 'systemd', 'dynamic linker', 'sshd', 'cron', 'sudo', 'kernel modules', 'writable root'];
const crates = ['rustls', 'quinn', 'h2', 'httparse', 'io-uring', 'wasmtime', 'mimalloc'];
---

<Section id="anatomy" eyebrow="Anatomy" title="Four layers. Nothing else in the image.">
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    Most server images are a general-purpose OS with a web server installed on top. liam drops the general-purpose OS
    and keeps only what serves requests. Linux handles the hardware. Rust does the rest.
  </Fragment>

  <ol class="stack">
    {
      layers.map((l) => (
        <li class:list={['layer', { hot: l.hot, base: l.base }]}>
          <div class="name">
            {l.name}
            <span>{l.sub}</span>
          </div>
          <p>{l.text}</p>
          <div class="size">
            {l.size}
            {l.sizeLabel && <span>{l.sizeLabel}</span>}
          </div>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>

  <div class="gone">
    <Cluster gap="2">
      <span class="lead">Not in the image:</span>
      {removed.map((r) => <s>{r}</s>)}
    </Cluster>
  </div>
  <p class="crates">
    You cannot exploit a shell that is not there, and you never patch a package you do not ship. Userspace is Rust end
    to end, built on {crates.map((c, i) => <><code>{c}</code>{i < crates.length - 2 ? ', ' : i === crates.length - 2 ? ' and ' : ''}</>)}.
    Every crate except the small, audited I/O core is <code>#![forbid(unsafe_code)]</code>.
  </p>
</Section>

<style>
  .stack {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  .layer {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 12rem minmax(0, 1fr) 7rem;
    gap: 20px;
    padding: 20px 22px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  .layer:first-child {
    border-top: 0;
  }

  .name {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .name span {
    display: block;
    font-weight: var(--weight-regular);
    font-size: var(--size-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .layer p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .size {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    text-align: right;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .size span {
    display: block;
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-mark);
  }

  .hot {
    background: var(--color-accent-soft);
  }

  .hot .name {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .base {
    background: transparent;
  }

  .gone {
    margin-top: 28px;
  }

  .lead {
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
    margin-right: 6px;
  }

  s {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    text-decoration-color: var(--color-mark);
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
    padding: 3px var(--space-2);
    border: 1px dashed var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .crates {
    margin-top: 20px;
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    max-width: 60em;
  }

  .crates code {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .layer {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .size {
      text-align: left;
    }
  }
</style>
